    "result_text": "The suite is green. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an `ageBand` derivation to `POST /api/owners`: when the request includes a `birthDate` (ISO), the created owner's response carries `ageBand` \u2014 `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+) \u2014 computed against its `registrationDate`.\n\nSince the pipeline persists the owner and the value is read back via a separate `GET`, `birthDate` had to be stored, and `ageBand` is derived at response-mapping time (matching how `locality`, `contactPreference`, etc. work).\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (input, `format: date`) to `OwnerFields`, and `ageBand` (readOnly string) to `Owner`. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n- **DB schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to `owners` (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field with getter/setter.\n- **`util/AgeBands.java`** (new) \u2014 `bandFor(owner)` computes the band from age at `registrationDate` via `Period.between`, returning `null` (so the field is omitted) when no `birthDate` was supplied.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapstruct expression wiring `ageBand` to `AgeBands.bandFor(owner)`.\n\nThe request's `birthDate` flows automatically: `ValidateOwnerFields` binds and republishes the body, `BuildOwner`'s `ownerMapper.toOwner(request)` maps `birthDate` by name (then `registrationDate` is set from the resolved business date), and `SaveOwner` persists it.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) and the full suite pass.",
